            </div>
        </div>


        <div class="sectors-cta">
            <a href="/services" class="text-link">SEE YOUR SOLUTIONS</a>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Social Proof Section -->
    <section class="testimonials-section">
        <div class="section-header reveal">
            <h2>Results</h2>
            <p>What clients have been able to do differently.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="testimonials-grid">
            <div class="testimonial-card reveal">
                <div class="testimonial-logo">
                    <img src="/logos/7skin.png" alt="7SKIN" width="164" height="96" loading="lazy">
                </div>
                <p class="testimonial-quote">"Our purchasing process ran in Excel with data pulled from 4 different systems, taking between 45 and 90 minutes per order cycle. Luís proposed a solution, validated it with us, and delivered a production platform the team now uses every day. Order decisions are now made from a single view, with data refreshed every 2 hours."</p>
                <div class="testimonial-author">
                    <strong>Rui Marques</strong>
                    <span>CEO, 7SKIN</span>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="testimonial-card reveal">
                <div class="testimonial-logo testimonial-logo--lg">
                    <img src="/logos/hephaesnus.png" alt="Hephaesnus" width="225" height="159" loading="lazy">
                </div>
                <p class="testimonial-quote">"Luís set up a complete e-commerce operation for our flagship product: payments, tax-compliant invoicing, and logistics, all automated, running across five European markets. It's still our production platform today, and now we run it ourselves, intuitively."</p>
                <div class="testimonial-author">
                    <strong>Henrique Bastos</strong>
                    <span>Hephaesnus</span>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="testimonial-card reveal">
                <div class="testimonial-logo">
                    <img src="/logos/portocar-care.png" alt="PortoCar Care" width="400" height="90" loading="lazy">
                </div>
                <p class="testimonial-quote">"We had always wanted to bring customers back based on the last service their car had. Now the system knows what each car had done and when, and handles that outreach on its own. 20% of bookings over the last six months came from it."</p>
                <div class="testimonial-author">
                    <strong>Pedro Pinto</strong>
                    <span>CEO, PortoCar Care</span>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- About Me Section -->
    <section id="about" class="about-section">
        <h2>ABOUT ME</h2>
        <div class="about-content reveal">
            <div class="about-intro">
                <h3>Two years in Venture Capital, evaluating business models across sectors.</h3>
            </div>
            <div class="about-description">
                <p>Understanding unit economics and the real pain points still shapes my initial approach to every project, before building the solution.</p>
                <a href="/about" class="text-link">MORE ABOUT ME</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Contact Section -->
    <section id="contact" class="contact-section-simple">
        <div class="contact-container reveal">
            <div class="cta-content">
                <h2>Let's talk about your business</h2>
                <p class="cta-subtext">Tell me what's slowing you down. I'll tell you what I can do about it.</p>
                <a href="/ai-contact" class="cta-button">Get in touch</a>
            </div>
            <div class="cta-background-text">LM</div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <script>
        // Mobile Menu Toggle
        const mobileMenuToggle = document.querySelector('.mobile-menu-toggle');
        const navLinks = document.querySelector('.nav-links');

        if (mobileMenuToggle) {
            mobileMenuToggle.addEventListener('click', () => {
                mobileMenuToggle.classList.toggle('active');
                navLinks.classList.toggle('active');
            });

            // Close menu when clicking on a link
            const links = navLinks.querySelectorAll('a');
            links.forEach(link => {
                link.addEventListener('click', () => {
                    mobileMenuToggle.classList.remove('active');
                    navLinks.classList.remove('active');
                });
            });
        }

        // Smooth scrolling for anchor links
        document.querySelectorAll('a[href^="#"]').forEach(anchor => {
            anchor.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
                e.preventDefault();
                const target = document.querySelector(this.getAttribute('href'));
                if (target) {
                    target.scrollIntoView({
                        behavior: 'smooth',
                        block: 'start'
                    });
                }
            });
        });

        // Add scroll effect to navigation
        let lastScroll = 0;
        const nav = document.querySelector('.navigation');

        window.addEventListener('scroll', () => {
            const currentScroll = window.pageYOffset;

            if (currentScroll > lastScroll && currentScroll > 100) {
                nav.style.transform = 'translateY(-100%)';
            } else {
                nav.style.transform = 'translateY(0)';
            }

            lastScroll = currentScroll;
        });

        // Scroll reveal (shared .reveal / .in-view utility from tokens.css)
        const revealEls = document.querySelectorAll(".reveal");
        if (revealEls.length && "IntersectionObserver" in window) {
            const revealIO = new IntersectionObserver(
                (entries) => {
                    entries.forEach((entry) => {
                        if (entry.isIntersecting) {
                            entry.target.classList.add("in-view");
                            revealIO.unobserve(entry.target);
                        }
                    });
                },
                { threshold: 0.12, rootMargin: "0px 0px -8% 0px" },
            );
            revealEls.forEach((el) => revealIO.observe(el));
        } else {
            revealEls.forEach((el) => el.classList.add("in-view"));
        }

        // Process rail: the timeline fill is a function of scroll position,
        // not a one-shot trigger, so it draws going down and retreats going
        // back up. Each step scales its own segment against a read line at
        // the middle of the viewport; the segments are contiguous, so they
        // paint as a single continuous line.
        const railRoot = document.querySelector(".process-rail");
        const railTracks = railRoot
            ? Array.from(railRoot.querySelectorAll(".rail-step")).map((step) => ({
                  step,
                  track: step.querySelector(".rail-track"),
              }))
            : [];
        const railReduceMotion = window.matchMedia(
            "(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)",
        ).matches;

        if (railRoot && railTracks.length && !railReduceMotion) {
            railRoot.classList.add("is-scrubbed");
            let railTicking = false;

            // A step is dimmed while its top sits low in the viewport and
            // reaches full strength as it climbs to the reading position, so
            // the next step previews itself before you arrive at it.
            const DIM = 0.16;
            const FOCUS_FROM = 0.9;
            const FOCUS_TO = 0.42;

            const updateRail = () => {
                railTicking = false;
                const viewport = window.innerHeight;
                const readLine = viewport / 2;
                const focusFrom = viewport * FOCUS_FROM;
                const focusTo = viewport * FOCUS_TO;
                railTracks.forEach(({ step, track }) => {
                    if (!track) return;
                    const rect = track.getBoundingClientRect();
                    if (!rect.height) return;

                    const progress = Math.min(
                        1,
                        Math.max(0, (readLine - rect.top) / rect.height),
                    );
                    track.style.setProperty("--rail-progress", progress.toFixed(4));
                    step.classList.toggle("is-reached", progress > 0);

                    const focus = Math.min(
                        1,
                        Math.max(0, (focusFrom - rect.top) / (focusFrom - focusTo)),
                    );
                    step.style.setProperty(
                        "--step-focus",
                        (DIM + (1 - DIM) * focus).toFixed(3),
                    );
                });
            };


            const queueRail = () => {
                if (railTicking) return;
                railTicking = true;
                requestAnimationFrame(updateRail);
            };

            updateRail();
            window.addEventListener("scroll", queueRail, { passive: true });
            window.addEventListener("resize", queueRail);
        }

        // Services: scope list drives one shared panel, cycling on its own.
        // The active scope's timer bar is the clock — its CSS animation ending
        // is what advances the panel. That means pausing the animation in CSS
        // (on hover or focus) pauses the cycle too, with no timer to manage,
        // and reduced-motion users get no animation and so no auto-advance.
        const svc = document.querySelector("[data-svc]");
        const svcTabs = svc ? Array.from(svc.querySelectorAll(".svc-scope")) : [];
        const svcPanels = svc ? Array.from(svc.querySelectorAll(".svc-panel")) : [];

        if (svc && svcTabs.length && svcTabs.length === svcPanels.length) {
            svc.classList.add("is-enhanced");
            let svcCurrent = 0;
            let svcCycling = true;

            const svcShow = (next) => {
                svcCurrent = (next + svcTabs.length) % svcTabs.length;
                svcTabs.forEach((tab, i) => {
                    const on = i === svcCurrent;
                    tab.classList.toggle("is-active", on);
                    tab.setAttribute("aria-selected", on ? "true" : "false");
                    tab.tabIndex = on ? 0 : -1;
                    svcPanels[i].classList.toggle("is-active", on);
                });
            };

            // Once the reader picks a scope, stop moving content under them.
            const svcStop = () => {
                svcCycling = false;
                svc.classList.remove("is-running");
            };

            svc.addEventListener("animationend", (event) => {
                if (svcCycling && event.target.classList.contains("svc-scope-timer")) {
                    svcShow(svcCurrent + 1);
                }
            });

            const svcStep = { ArrowDown: 1, ArrowRight: 1, ArrowUp: -1, ArrowLeft: -1 };

            svcTabs.forEach((tab, i) => {
                tab.addEventListener("click", () => {
                    svcStop();
                    svcShow(i);
                });
                tab.addEventListener("keydown", (event) => {
                    let target = null;
                    if (event.key in svcStep) target = svcCurrent + svcStep[event.key];
                    else if (event.key === "Home") target = 0;
                    else if (event.key === "End") target = svcTabs.length - 1;
                    if (target === null) return;
                    event.preventDefault();
                    svcStop();
                    svcShow(target);
                    svcTabs[svcCurrent].focus();
                });
            });

            // Only cycle while the section is on screen, so the reader does not
            // arrive to find it already three panels in.
            if ("IntersectionObserver" in window) {
                const svcIO = new IntersectionObserver(
                    (entries) => {
                        entries.forEach((entry) => {
                            if (svcCycling) {
                                svc.classList.toggle("is-running", entry.isIntersecting);
                            }
                        });
                    },
                    { threshold: 0.35 },
                );
                svcIO.observe(svc);
            } else {
                svc.classList.add("is-running");
            }

            svcShow(0);
        }
    </script>

